# Root ignores only. Each project keeps its own .gitignore and those are the
# authority on their own build output.
#
# Deliberately NOT a concatenation of the six. A leading slash in a .gitignore
# anchors to the directory containing that file, not to the repository root, so
# the six sibling files already mean exactly what they meant as repo roots.
# Merging them here would push poketrack's `venv/`, `*pyc*` and `.yarn/*` over
# every project, and hub's `work/` would swallow any directory named `work`
# anywhere in the tree.

# Never
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

.DS_Store
